---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaSlice from '../../components/CtaSlice.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Vibe"
  description="What Limber is really about — joyful movement, real community, and a place to feel at home in your body."
>

  <!-- ── OUR VIBE — split hero ── -->
  <section class="border-b-2 border-neutral-900 lg:flex" style="min-height: 80vh;">

    <!-- Left: heading + copy + pillars -->
    <div class="lg:w-1/2 bg-limber-green flex flex-col justify-center px-8 lg:px-14 py-16 lg:py-20">
      <h1 class="leading-tight mb-10">
        <span class="font-headline uppercase text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-limber-cream">our </span><em class="font-display uppercase not-italic italic font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-limber-vibe">vibe.</em>
      </h1>

      <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-limber-vibe leading-snug mb-4">
        looking for a place that genuinely knows you, celebrates the wins big and small embarrassingly loud, and where community actually means something?
      </p>
      <p class="font-headline text-xl text-limber-cream mb-6">you just found your people…</p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-8">
        <p class="font-sans text-limber-cream/70 leading-relaxed">
          when we opened limber, we wanted to bring movement back to what it should be — something you love, not a chore, not a thing to always measure or a tool to punish.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-limber-cream/70 leading-relaxed">
          a place where community is genuinely valued and not just a word on a website.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-limber-cream/70 leading-relaxed">
          no pressure. no expectations. just space to move in a way that feels good for you.
        </p>
        <p class="font-sans text-limber-cream/70 leading-relaxed">
          because movement isn't just exercise — it's a moment of joy, connection, and a gift.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-8 border-t border-limber-cream/20">
        {['Belonging.', 'Joyful movement.', 'Embodied wellbeing.'].map((pillar) => (
          <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-limber-cream/80 py-4 border-b border-limber-cream/20">{pillar}</p>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="font-sans text-xs text-limber-cream/40 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">our mission</p>
      <p class="font-display italic text-lg text-limber-vibe leading-snug">
        to help people feel at home in their bodies.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Right: image -->
    <div class="lg:w-1/2 flex-shrink-0">
      <img
        src="/images/Limber_April26_102.jpg"
        alt="Limber studio"
        class="w-full h-64 lg:h-full object-cover border-t-2 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l-2 border-neutral-900"
      />
    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- ── THE STARTING POINT ── -->
  <section class="bg-limber-cream py-20 lg:py-28 border-b-2 border-neutral-900">
    <div class="px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

      <!-- Heading -->
      <h2 class="mb-12">
        <span class="font-headline uppercase text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-limber-green block leading-none mb-1">the starting</span>
        <em class="font-display uppercase not-italic italic font-medium text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl text-limber-tericotta block leading-none">point</em>
      </h2>

      <!-- Letter + photo -->
      <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16 items-start">

        <!-- Letter -->
        <div class="space-y-5">
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            before this studio had walls, it had a pub. a surf club. a library. a railway hall. honestly, the list goes on.
          </p>
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            for two years i taught as limber with lily across whatever spaces would have me — building from one class to fifteen, person by person. i was new to the area, still finding my feet. and if i'm really honest, i was trying to build a community for myself just as much as anyone else.
          </p>
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            in 2024 a spot came up in thirroul plaza. a little old, a little tired, with a bit of a reputation.
          </p>
          <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-limber-tericotta leading-snug">
            i saw potential. was i crazy? maybe. my gut said otherwise. boy, i'm glad i listened.
          </p>
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            i danced professionally for years. and honestly — it made me fall completely out of love with movement. i spent so long measuring myself, competing, being judged. my body became something to manage, not something to live in.
          </p>
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            when i found pilates i fell back in love with movement. properly. it healed me. but it also gave me a completely different lens — movement stopped being something to compete with or be judged on. it became simply mine.
          </p>
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            i looked at the fitness industry around me and saw the same patterns playing out. people comparing, picking themselves apart, chasing an aesthetic that — trust me, i know from personal experience — won't make them happy when they reach it.
          </p>
          <p class="font-display italic text-xl text-limber-tericotta leading-snug">
            i never wanted to create a studio that did that. if i had, i would have failed.
          </p>
          <p class="font-sans text-limber-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            limber exists to give people back what movement is actually supposed to be — joyful, healing, freeing. a place to stop the head noise. to be present. to stop wasting energy tearing yourself down.
          </p>

          <!-- Sign-off -->
          <p class="font-headline text-sm text-limber-tericotta pt-4">lily, founder 🖤</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Lily photo -->
        <div class="mt-12 lg:mt-0 lg:sticky lg:top-28">
          <img
            src="/images/Limber_April26_168.jpg"
            alt="Lily, founder of Limber"
            class="w-full h-[480px] lg:h-[600px] object-cover rounded-2xl border-2 border-neutral-900"
          />
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSlice
    headingLine1="ready to"
    headingLine2="find your people?"
    body="come say hi, book a class, or just have a nosy around. we'd love to have you."
    image="/images/Limber_April26_176.jpg"
    imageAlt="Limber community"
    buttons={[
      { label: 'meet our tribe', href: '/about/our-tribe' },
      { label: 'see our classes', href: '/classes/our-classes', variant: 'outline' },
    ]}
  />

</BaseLayout>
